WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.734
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.067
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:07.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.467
Guys, it seems like there's
so much going on right now.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:15.100
This weekend, President Biden
tested positive again for COVID.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.033
Yeah. Someone in Illinois won

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:19.868
the $1.3 billion
Mega Millions jackpot.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:22.734
Tonight was a new episode of
"The Bachelorette."

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:27.167
And Applebee's is selling
chicken-wing-flavored lip gloss.

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:32.400
There's a lot to go over.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.200
Let's just jump in,
cover it all at once.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.367
It's time for "News Smash."
Here we go.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:39.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.467
[ Ding ]

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:44.234
First up, after testing negative
for COVID last week,

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.834
President Biden
has tested positive again

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.634
in a rebound case.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:51.267
Wow. The odds of that happening
are like one in a...

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:54.901
billion. That's how much cash

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.801
the Mega Millions winner
is taking home.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:59.267
With a bank account like that,
they'll never have a job again,

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.467
kind of like...

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:03.667
every contestant on
"The Bachelorette."

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:06.667
Gabby and Rachel have narrowed
it down to about a dozen guys.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:09.000
They've come on --
They went on dates to Paris.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.400
They flew on helicopters.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.067
Unlike the real world, where
your first date is usually at...

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.601
Applebee's.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:19.701
They're making an all-new
chicken-wing-flavored lip gloss.

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.400
The only way you're going to
want to slather that

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.701
on your lips is if you...

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.100
can't taste or smell.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.133
COVID...

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:31.434
It's hard for Biden.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:33.400
It's no fun
being isolated and alone

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.267
when you're someone who's so...

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.334
Gabby.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.868
Will she get her man or will
Rachel swoop in and steal him?

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.434
Pretty soon, they'll be off to

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.100
the Fantasy Suite,
trying to get...

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.567
lucky.

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:47.000
Imagine your friend winning
the lottery.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.067
If you were ever mean to them,

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.634
then it's definitely time
for you to...

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:51.067
pucker up.

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.868
Seriously, chicken-wing lip
gloss from a chain restaurant?

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:56.601
I mean, rubbing that on your
face -- it feels like a real...

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:57.634
gamble.

00:01:57.634 --> 00:02:00.234
And the winner is
sure glad they did,

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.601
but you know they were at home

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:04.067
double-, triple-, and
quadruple-checking just to be...

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:07.868
positive. When he found out
that he's still contagious,

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:11.300
Biden got sent home alone in a
limo, just like the loser on...

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.067
"The Bachelorette."

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:15.868
The winners get the girls, while
the losers might as well be...

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.133
boneless.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.267
So, in conclusion...

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:20.701
get a rose...

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.100
that blows...

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.534
so close...

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.067
so gross.

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:26.601
This has been a "News Smash."

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:28.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.501
That's right. That's right.

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:34.934
Over the weekend,
President Biden

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:38.534
returned to isolation after once
again testing positive for COVID

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:41.133
in what his doctor called
a rebound case.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.000
Right now, Biden's looking on
the bright side.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.467
He's like, "Well, at least my
COVID got a second term."

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.400
That's right --
a rebound case of COVID.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.868
Usually when a 79-year-old
is on the rebound,

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:59.367
you're meeting your
new aunt named Barbara.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:01.100
That's right --
the virus came back so fast,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.667
staffers didn't even
have time to take down the

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:03.834
"get well soon" balloons.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.434
They're like, "Wait.
You just..."

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:07.868
Luckily, Biden's doing okay.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.667
He's back to
binge-watching "Matlock"

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.200
right where he left off.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.634
Biden has COVID again.

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:16.434
He was positive, then negative,
now he's back to positive.

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.033
They're saying it's
'cause of the medicine he took,

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:19.701
but I think it might be
something else.

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:21.734
Watch this commercial
I saw the other day.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.968
-[ Russian accent ]
Do you love practical joke?

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:27.033
Then pick up Vladimir Putin's
Trick COVID Test,

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:29.000
the only test that trick you.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.200
[ Laughs ]

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.400
It's a positive, then negative,

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.701
then positive, then negative,

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:38.033
then monkeypox, then pregnant.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:40.534
Vladimir Putin's
Trick COVID Test.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:43.334
Used by White House,
and they don't even know.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:46.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Isn't that amazing?

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.767
He's selling trick COVID tests.
-Wow!

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:55.634
-Speaking of COVID,
The White House

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:58.067
is planning to offer
updated booster shots

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:00.100
to Americans this fall.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.300
Yep, it's still
the same booster,

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.968
except these are gonna be
pumpkin spice.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.000
Meanwhile, this weekend,
former president Trump

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.200
was busy hosting
the Saudi Arabia-backed

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.267
LIV golf tournament at his club
in New Jersey.

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:13.367
And I saw a photo of him singing
the national anthem

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:14.367
I thought was funny.

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:15.400
Look at this.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.501
There he is.
-Oh.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.267
Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.434
-Yeah, he's either singing
the national anthem

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:24.667
or burping up a hot dog.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.400
I don't know what...

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.334
But this is fun.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.567
If you hit a golf ball in his
mouth, you win a free round.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:31.601
-Really?
-Isn't that fun?

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.334
I think it's cool.

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.767
Well, it was a life-changing
weekend for the person

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.501
in Illinois who purchased
the winning ticket

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:40.467
for the $1.3 billion
Mega Millions jackpot.

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:42.067
The winner hasn't
come forward yet,

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.267
so either they're contacting
financial experts

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.801
or they're at home like,
"Crap, where is it?

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.367
Alright, I had it in my --
I went swimming.

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:48.534
I went swimming. Oh, wait.

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:50.367
No one turn on
the washing machine!

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.133
No one do anything.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.133
No one do anything.
Where was it?

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:00.501
I had it --
Why do shirts have pockets?

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.167
Too many pockets!"

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:04.801
But it's a great story.

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:06.634
I mean,
one person hit the Mega --

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:09.100
That's a lot of money
right there, $1.3 billion.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.834
I mean, I played.
I only got one number.

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:13.133
Tariq, how about you?

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:16.000
-I didn't play.
The odds are a trillion-to-one.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.167
And what?

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.868
Am I supposed to believe
that I have a chance?

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.434
Like if I pick --
I don't know --

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.267
13 for my wife's birthday,

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:24.467
and then, like, 36 and 45

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:26.934
because those are the
two streets I lived on as a kid,

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.934
and then 57 and 67

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:31.834
because they're the uniform
numbers of my favorite athletes,

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:33.734
and then 14
because it's my lucky number?

00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:35.634
[ Laughs ] Please.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.167
-Uh, Tariq, 13, 36, 45, 57, 67,

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:45.100
and 14 were the winning numbers.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:48.067
-Um, I'm sorry.
What's this, now?

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:51.267
-You just randomly selected
the numbers

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:53.968
that would have won you
over a billion dollars.

00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:56.567
-Uh, will you excuse me?

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.267
[Bleep]

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:03.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:10.267
I'm, um, happy for the winner.

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:12.534
-Yeah, yeah, good.
Yeah, nice of you. Wow.

00:06:12.534 --> 00:06:14.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:20.033
Yeah, the chase for the big
Mega Millions prize is over now,

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:22.534
but that hasn't stopped
reporters from telling us

00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:25.834
just how unlikely it was that
we would have ever won this.

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:27.200
Listen to this.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.334
-The odds of winning were
astronomical, 1-in-303 million.

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:32.801
-According to some experts,
you are nearly

00:06:32.801 --> 00:06:35.200
three times more likely
to be killed by

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.200
a vending-machine-related
accident.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.234
-You're more likely to be
hit by a meteorite.

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:41.634
-You have better odds of being
struck by lightning.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.667
-You are more likely to be
killed by

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:46.667
a swarm of bees or hornets.

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.601
-You had a better chance of
having a

00:06:48.601 --> 00:06:51.667
"toilet-related injury,"
whatever that means.

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:56.067
-A toilet-related...
-Toilet-related injury?

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:58.167
-With the vending machine?

00:06:58.167 --> 00:06:59.634
The odds of getting
struck by lightning

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:02.634
on a toilet must be insane.

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:05.334
Switching gears, on Saturday,
Pope Francis acknowledged

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:08.167
that he will need to
slow down or retire.

00:07:08.167 --> 00:07:10.701
So I guess we know who won
the Mega Millions.

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:13.701
Congratulations, Your Holiness.

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:15.334
You can tell the pope
is ready to retire.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.167
Today, someone asked him
for a miracle,

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:18.400
and he was like,
"What do I look like?

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.501
A freaking genie over here?"

00:07:24.133 --> 00:07:25.300
Some business news.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:26.868
I read that, today,
the C.E.O. of

00:07:26.868 --> 00:07:29.400
Carnival Cruise Line
has stepped down.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.334
Yeah, apparently, he was tired
of being in charge of

00:07:31.334 --> 00:07:34.667
toilet-related injuries.

00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:36.067
Some entertainment news.

00:07:36.067 --> 00:07:40.067
Disney+ is working on a
live-action "Eragon" TV series.

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:42.801
-Ooh!
-Yeah. It's pretty exciting.

00:07:42.801 --> 00:07:44.834
Yeah, here's the trailer for it.

00:07:44.834 --> 00:07:49.334
-"Eragon," the most popular
books of 2002.

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:51.834
Now, just 20 short years later,

00:07:51.834 --> 00:07:54.667
it's finally time for
this beloved series about...

00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:55.901
[ Record scratches ]
...horses or, like, frogs?

00:07:55.901 --> 00:07:58.467
[ Frog croaks ]
Or was it unicorns? I forget.

00:07:58.467 --> 00:08:02.100
"Eragon" --
prepare to be reminded.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.734
-Wow. Amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:04.734 --> 00:08:06.434
What was that about?

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:10.734
Guys, did you see this video of
passengers on a

00:08:10.734 --> 00:08:13.534
Frontier Airlines flight
being sprayed with

00:08:13.534 --> 00:08:16.667
some "refreshing mist,"
apparently?

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:19.434
It's a thing they do.
But this looks a little thick.

00:08:19.434 --> 00:08:20.467
Check this out.

00:08:20.467 --> 00:08:23.701
-Wow!

00:08:23.701 --> 00:08:25.200
-Yo!

00:08:28.434 --> 00:08:29.901
Wow.

00:08:31.367 --> 00:08:33.033
Yeah. Wow.

00:08:33.033 --> 00:08:36.901
They call this the "vegetable
aisle at Kroger experience."

00:08:37.868 --> 00:08:39.567
It's the first time
a flight's been delayed

00:08:39.567 --> 00:08:42.033
because of bad weather
inside the plane.

00:08:42.734 --> 00:08:44.834
And, yet, somehow,
the chicken was still dry.

00:08:44.834 --> 00:08:45.934
Isn't that unbelievable?

00:08:47.133 --> 00:08:49.200
Guys, finally, you ever see
a photo in the news

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.567
and think, "That headline
should be different"?

00:08:50.567 --> 00:08:51.767
Well, we'll take care of that
right now.

00:08:51.767 --> 00:08:53.734
It's time for
"News and Improved."

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:55.801
Here we go.
♪♪

00:08:55.801 --> 00:09:01.234
-♪ News and Improved ♪

00:09:01.234 --> 00:09:03.767
-For example,
check out this first photo.

00:09:03.767 --> 00:09:04.868
The original headline was...

00:09:08.067 --> 00:09:09.767
That headline can definitely
be improved,

00:09:09.767 --> 00:09:11.334
because if you only looked
at the photo,

00:09:11.334 --> 00:09:12.567
the headline could have been...

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:19.167 --> 00:09:20.701
Up next, this headline says...

00:09:24.334 --> 00:09:25.400
Headline could have been...

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:31.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:32.634 --> 00:09:33.634
Next headline was...

00:09:36.767 --> 00:09:37.767
Headline could have been...

00:09:40.968 --> 00:09:43.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:43.567 --> 00:09:46.868
-Eh!
-Next headline was...

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.300
Headline could have been...

00:09:55.667 --> 00:09:58.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:58.667 --> 00:10:00.133
Wow.

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:03.067
Next headline was...

00:10:06.634 --> 00:10:07.767
Headline could have been...

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:15.267
"What else is going --
What else is going on?"

00:10:15.267 --> 00:10:16.300
This next headline was...

00:10:19.467 --> 00:10:20.467
Headline could have been...

00:10:24.467 --> 00:10:27.434
I'd check that out.

00:10:27.434 --> 00:10:28.667
And, finally,
this headline was...

00:10:31.701 --> 00:10:32.701
Headline could have been...

00:10:35.033 --> 00:10:36.634
That's all we have
for "News and Improved."

00:10:36.634 --> 00:10:37.634
We have a great show.

